n","Independent foundation review outcome"],"review":{"targets":["T01","T02","T03"],"requiredReviewers":["agent:independent-foundation-review"],"mandatoryChecks":["npm run test:all","Import/restart/MCP acceptance"],"approved":false}},{"id":"T04","parentId":"MVP","title":"Build the independent-column Tasks board","purpose":"development","state":"backlog","dependencies":["R02"],"goal":"Make real inputs and task placements readable and minimally editable.","scope":["Inputs / Backlog / Queued / Running / Blocked columns with independent layout.","Root-only backlog, priority groups, selection, breadcrumb and simple persisted create/move actions.","No speculative toolbar or drag-only overlay.","Audit existing table and header components. Reuse/extract header pieces and compose independent column content/scroll; document the chosen shared boundary."],"successCriteria":["Board is populated from persisted real data, not mockup fixtures.","Backlog contains only parentless tasks; priorities are ordered 0..n and editable without drag.","Columns have no common row grid; selection and scroll survive unrelated updates.","Right side stays blank without a selection, and selected task can open its graph."],"evidenceRequired":["Focused board browser tests","Desktop/narrow screenshots","Real create/move/readback demo"]},{"id":"T05","parentId":"MVP","title":"Build the model-faithful nested task graph timeline","purpose":"development","state":"backlog","dependencies":["R02"],"goal":"Show the actual plan and recorded work without flattening relationships.","scope":["Reusable graph projection/renderer with containment drill-down and actual prerequisites.","Schematic planned/recorded task ranges and queue episodes, parallel paths, integration, review end dots and abandoned branches; chronology without measured durations.","Participant metadata only where actually known. No duration/cost features."],"successCriteria":["Every visible task/edge maps to real persisted IDs and their actual relationship; outside-scope prerequisites are reachable.","Nested tasks can be opened through breadcrumb; shared nodes are not duplicated as independent tasks.","Planned versus recorded work and incomplete versus complete attempts are distinguishable; range length is not measured time and chronology/relations remain faithful.","No duration/cost fields, placeholders, elapsed axis or breakdown; graph connectors have no arrows and labels remain unboxed.","The golden loop topology has distinct task IDs and only its declared edges; failed review end returns downward to next work start, each range has two caps, abandoned review is terminal, and parallel work/reviews remain possible.","Known queue episodes render gray without numeric duration; participation differs according to actual actor data and no unknown actors are fabricated."],"evidenceRequired":["Graph projection tests","Branch/replan/abandon browser scenarios","Visual screenshots with data references"]},{"id":"T06","parentId":"MVP","title":"Compose complete UI CRUD and review controls","purpose":"development","state":"backlog","dependencies":["T04","T05"],"goal":"Let the user perform every supported planning operation independently through reusable UI components.","scope":["Implement every UI/MCP parity row using existing controls, targeted rework and approved shared additions.","Use the reviewed V1-V4 layouts for task/input relationships, queue/state actions, evidence and review.","Include create/delete, link/unlink, priorities, import/export and structured conflict/error handling.","Implement schema/reflection-driven Node view and one view matching adapter over existing types/fields/relations.","Reuse persisted graph-reference resolution and existing navigation; implement node revision comparison with shared controls. New URL UI is excluded.","Compose shared Review tabs, Author readiness, grouped-feedback display/composer, single-column Checks hierarchy and shared selection/toolbar components. Integrate existing files/diff/Preview views without custom substitutes."],"successCriteria":["Every exposed planning tool operation has a tested, discoverable UI path; no routine operation requires Codex or hand-edited JSON.","UI and MCP use identical owning operation contracts and actor-specific restrictions.","No surface-specific form, selector, command menu, thread widget or graph renderer duplicates a reusable component.","Unselected panel is blank; keyboard/focus/draft behavior survives unrelated updates.","Node works for editable and read-only nodes; creator is a read-only relation. No schema-specific task screen duplicates the shared renderer.","Node and evidence navigation resolve deserialized graph links to the correct target/revision using existing contracts; missing/deleted targets are explicit. No new URL UI or external browser-entry acceptance requirement.","No/inline/side-by-side comparison handles fields and relations. Historical read-only selection never changes expectedRevision for live writes.","Review has Overview/Changes/Preview, Author readiness and Checks -> Reviewers/Runnables -> Mandatory/Optional. Four right-aligned Runnables tree-row actions operate highlights; no checkboxes, per-item play controls, duplicate outcome/action panels or URL strip.","Both new comments and replies use the same editable typed-row component with row removal, clear boundaries and bottom actions; top-level content spans available width and replies alone indent.","Changes exposes all/modified files and exact target/composed iteration diff, line-anchored feedback and Preview reuse; view switching preserves unrelated panel state.","Runnables is an ordinary nested row under Checks; the Overview inner splitter begins below the toolbar and every far-right view tool remains inside the toolbar spanning both subpanes."],"evidenceRequired":["UI/MCP parity acceptance matrix","V1-V4 browser screenshots","Independent user CRUD walkthrough"]},{"id":"T07","parentId":"MVP","title":"Connect real evidence and review gates","purpose":"integration","state":"backlog","dependencies":["R02"],"goal":"Make review and observation work with actual results rather than sample content.","scope":["Reuse session/turn-range, current diff, captured snapshot and check-run evidence.","Review ordinary tasks against definitions/results or exact code snapshots; support blocked/revise/approve/abandon outcomes.","Keep reviewed scope frozen, block dependants and preserve independent work choices.","Project automatic/semantic/deterministic requirements and author-owned comment closure into a unified review check collection; requirement provenance and submitted revision are retained.","Build on the basic gate enforcement delivered in T01/T02 for R02; integrate richer file/session/check evidence and unified presentation without creating a second owner.","Detect/aggregate existing repository-owned checks and wire one granular run-checks operation through shared UI/MCP; attach existing coverage/report evidence without building the shared-check framework.","Adapt freshness gates so the human can explicitly accept an earlier passed run for the selected revision; show both the mismatch and acceptance, never a fabricated fresh pass.","Wire header run-all/mandatory/selected and scoped cancellation to the shared check owner; preserve partial evidence and distinguish unsupported cancellation."],"successCriteria":["Planning-only review does not require a fake Git diff or code checks.","Code review shows the exact submitted revision and run provenance. Stale results are flagged and block passage unless the human records target-specific acceptance of earlier passed evidence; changed snapshot identity is never silently substituted.","All comments must close and all required reviewers approve; generic edits cannot bypass gates.","Sessions may span attempts via turn ranges; evidence links open the correct existing viewer.","Shared checkout limits are visible, without falsely promising automatic parallel isolation.","Reviewer decisions and comment/input closure derive from their owners. Generic metadata changes cannot manufacture passage; open comments remain blocking. Stale passed evidence can be accepted only by an explicit human decision bound to the target revision.","One run-checks call resolves repository-owned applicable checks at the requested granularity and aggregates their results without requiring the agent to choose individual commands.","Execution record distinguishes selected/run/skipped/not-run checks, versions and when each ran. Later changes preserve the old result and reveal the mismatch.","Coverage exposes measured result and effective threshold with available scope/provenance. No line/file/function coverage explorer, shared pipeline engine or agent-review harness is required.","All/mandatory/selected deduplicate runnable targets and never invoke reviewer/closure rows. Stop records affected run IDs and observed cancellation/partial results; cancelled/missing evidence never becomes mandatory pass.","Latest nested check evidence and chronological run events reference the same stored execution; neither rewrites policy or hides stale results.","Failed-R02 replacement scenario passes end to end, including required-actor finish boundary, overlapping freeze protection, unresolved comment carry-forward and no generic-unlink gate bypass."],"evidenceRequired":["Review/evidence integration tests","Blocked-dependant and snapshot mismatch demonstrations"]},{"id":"T08","parentId":"MVP","title":"Integrate the surfaces and complete the usage walkthrough","purpose":"integration","state":"backlog","dependencies":["T06","T07"],"goal":"Finish a small usable release and remove replaced UI/data paths.","scope":["Wire both surfaces, inspector and tools together against the imported real plan.","Remove superseded sample fallback and duplicate old entry points within replaced scope.","Run the acceptance scenario, inspect screenshots and record issues as inputs/tasks."],"suc