encies":[],"goal":"Let Broccoli, templates and other repositories reuse check infrastructure without copying pipelines, preserving exact definition versions and applicability.","scope":["Identify reusable parts of the Broccoli testing system and template integration needs.","Design code/API-defined versioned checks/pipelines and choose a linking/pinning approach from evidence; Git submodules are an option, not a decision.","Check/provider-owned applicability predicates with an explicit escape hatch when conventions conflict.","Expose semantic capabilities through portable tools first; avoid dependence on Codex-specific hooks.","Coverage evidence with computed and literal threshold provenance and system/file/function scope for critical code."],"successCriteria":["A shared check can serve Broccoli and a template without duplicated test-system implementation.","Runs identify the exact shared definition revision, target version and applicability reasoning; updates do not rewrite old results.","A user can force a check where conventions miss it, with the override visible.","Coverage reports distinguish measured values from thresholds, show how each threshold was obtained or overridden and expose relevant file/function coverage.","Follow-up scope and implementation are reviewed separately; this task is not a dependency or completion criterion of the current MVP."],"evidenceRequired":["Reusable check API and versioning proposal","Broccoli/template example","Applicability and coverage policy examples"]}],"reviewPolicy":{"sequence":["Independent software-design review","Implementation self-check and independent foundation review","Independent implementation review","User acceptance in the running app"],"requiredReviewers":["Per-checkpoint policy: independent agent for SD01/R02, human:user for R03"],"agentRole":"Latest user instruction explicitly authorizes independent design and implementation reviewers and continued implementation after intermediate agent-verified gates. This does not authorize impersonation of a human or automatic product agent orchestration. R03 requires the real user.","comments":"Every root discussion must close before passage, regardless of its feedback types. Root author owns close/reopen; each input/reply author owns permitted text edits/removals. Replies retain attribution but do not create independent closure gates. Amendments never silently close a root discussion. Derived Comments closed is not independently toggled; unresolved decisions block. Carry unresolved discussions by reference across replacement review tasks.","iteration":"Freeze reviewed-scope implementation during submitted review. After all required reviewers finish with changes requested, release that review's freeze (other overlapping freezes remain). Explicitly create a NEW continuation work task; later explicitly create a NEW draft review. Exact target is captured on submission, not when future work is created. Link lineage and transfer pending dependency gates explicitly as in Review progression, freeze and successor gates. No automatic execution or independent-branch pausing.","disposition":"Approve -> pass if checks/comments allow; request changes -> next scoped work iteration; pending decision -> blocked with dependants blocked; abandon -> terminate. Independent tasks pause only by explicit choice. Once passed, that review result and threads are sealed. Further concerns require a fresh related review task; no retroactive rewrite or automatic rollback of completed dependent work.","bootstrap":"R01 records accepted design history. SD01 verifies concrete software design. R02 independently verifies persisted state, MCP and the human action path using test principals; it requires no overnight user pause. R03 is actual user acceptance through the full UI. Imported policy must preserve these explicitly attributed delivery amendments."},"handoff":["Keep this plan pack as the bootstrap authority until T03 can import through the domain service.","Dry-run the intake first, validate IDs, links, parent/dependency cycles, reviewer identities and criteria. Do not execute anything or fabricate history from planned work.","Atomically import tasks, review requirements, dependencies and descriptions plus the complete approved specification and immutable source snapshot/evidence manifest. Copy locally stored reference images/annotations into app-owned evidence or verify an equally durable owned attachment; no temp-only screenshot references after retirement. Preserve stable bootstrap IDs as source references and map to app IDs. Bootstrap scope/goals/criteria become freeform description text, not extra application schema fields.","Read back every task, description, relation, review gate and all cross-cutting contracts/corrections/deferred scope. Verify immutable source/artifact hashes and image availability, restart and repeat. Transfer authority only if the full specification survives; a hash without retrievable content is insufficient. A retry must not duplicate records.","Write IMPORT-RECEIPT.json containing source hash, import request ID, app context/root task ID, ID mapping, committed revision and verification result. The receipt contains no credentials.","After verification, replace temporary plan.json and PLAN.md with the receipt/link notice and remove this temporary generator. Do not maintain two editable plans. All remaining progress/plan changes go through app tools/UI.","If import fails, leave the pack authoritative and unchanged; report a structured error. No silent fallback to sample data or direct JSON-store editing.","Import B01 as a separate root backlog task outside MVP containment/dependencies. Preserve its follow-up needs; do not require its completion for R03."],"acceptanceScenario":["Open the imported MVP root, read its description and pending tasks, create a title-only child, revise its freeform description and add one prerequisite through the UI.","From Broccoli Local MCP tools in Codex, update that same child using its revision, attach an issue input without confirming its classification, and read it back in both surfaces.","Queue a selected task while atomically creating priority0, insert a second bracket with another selected task, reorder priorities, and move tasks through backlog/queued/blocked/back. Removing the last member removes that bracket. No agent/model request starts.","Open the parent graph and inspect nested tasks, shared/parallel prerequisites, planned work and a recorded prior attempt. Change a plan and verify the prior definition is still inspectable.","Open linked real session/current diff where available and distinguish it from the submitted snapshot. Missing evidence is explicit. No duration or cost fields/placeholders are present.","Submit a planning-only review and a code-snapshot review. Add Fix/Explain/Suggestion/Propose comments; verify open comments, missing approval and stale mandatory checks prevent passage. Agent cannot close the human thread or approve as the human.","Record changes requested after required reviewers finish, release only that review's freeze and create a distinct continuation work task. Later create a separate draft review, replace enumerated pending review gate edges and submit its exact new target. Fold the return edge; retain old task/result and unresolved discussion references.","Restart, return via the breadcrumb/deep link, and confirm data/history/review state survived. Reject a stale write. Create and delete a disposable unreferenced task from each mutation surface.","Use the app to amend at least one real remaining MVP task and close the final review. This is the switch from demonstrating the surface to actually using it.","Perform the complete CRUD operation matrix in the UI without agent assistance, including input/task deletion, relationship unlinking, priority changes and import/export; verify all effects through MCP readback.","Open Node for a read-only node and an editable task; inspect creator in flat relations. Switch to Review where supported, preserving context without remounting unrelated panels.","Compare two saved revisions in no/inline/side-by-side modes including a text change and relation addition/removal. Verify no edit controls target a historical snapshot.","Persist/export graph references, discard in-memory objects, deserialize/restart with a changed runtime binding and navigate to the same node/review/evidence revision through existing reference controls. Include shared, missing and deleted targets; prove identity is not an origin/port or object-instance alias. No new browser URL UI is required.","Inspect Checks -> Reviewers/Runnables -> Mandatory/Optional. Configure requirements through Node before submission; act on human outcome in its row. Multi-select executable runnable leaves and invoke all/mandatory/selected/stop from the right side of the Runnables tree row; no per-item or footer run controls.","Run change-relevant repository checks through a single MCP call and corresponding UI operation. Inspect per-repository aggregation, definition revisions, selected/run/skipped/not-run status and existing coverage artifacts. Request full-suite/performance granularity only explicitly.","Modify code after a passed run. The old result remains visible as stale; agent cannot waive that fact. Human can record acceptance of this earlier passed evidence for the new review target with a reason, or request a rerun. Failed/never-run required tests cannot be silently waived.","As author, prepare a draft review and explanatory multi-row comment. Submit it, then prove target/policy edits and implementation writes are frozen while discussion and observation checks remain available.","Add/remove typed feedback rows in new comments and replies; verify shared component layout, full-width top-level context and Overview preview. Another actor cannot delete or close human feedback; removal does not bypass closure and restart preserves changes.","Switch Overview/Changes/Preview repeatedly without resetting graph selection/scroll, comments, tree selection or drafts. Inspect exact submitted code, switch All/Modified, open context from an anchored comment, and detect unavailable historical preview honestly.","Select several iteration diffs, verify composed changes include only selected work and conflict handling; graph selection of one iteration updates that same control. Historical source and comments remain bound to immutable targets.","Run two disjoint selected check leaves plus their parent and verify no duplicate executions. Stop the resulting run group, inspect partial/cancelled state through UI/MCP, and prove it cannot satisfy mandatory success.","Exercise rejected R02 -> correction task -> replacement R02b: T04 remains blocked after R02 rejects and after R02b is created/submitted; T04 becomes eligible only after the authorized gate replacement and R02b passage. R02 stays non-passing; original open comments still block R02b until author-closed. Generic deletion/unlink cannot bypass this gate.","Hold two overlapping submitted reviews, finish one with changes requested and prove the other freeze remains. Block a required reviewer decision and prove freeze/gate remain; then resolve explicitly. Abandon a branch and prove its downstream prerequisites never become passed."],"verification":["Planning pack: mechanically verify unique IDs, existing parents/prerequisites, acyclic task and prerequisite graphs, review targets/gates, nonempty success criteria, no fabricated implementation completions and existence of cited source/image paths.","Storage/domain: title-only tasks, nesting/prerequisites, shared references, priorities, actor rights, stale writes, failed transaction recovery, idempotent imports, restart and deletion safety.","Tools: real existing-plugin discovery and deterministic contributor/MCP CRUD round trips, then Codex tool read/write/readback; two writers, import retry, actor restrictions and no execution side effects. UI tests cover the same operation matrix.","UI: focused Playwright tests for each changed behavior, browser reload/restart persistence, independently scrolling columns, breadcrumb navigation, faithful branches, selection/focus/draft retention, keyboard access and readable narrow layout.","Reviews: immutable revision targeting, all comments closed, required actor approval, current mandatory checks, blocked dependants and next-iteration transition.","At each implementation review checkpoint: npm run test:all from active repo (root build + Node tests + browser tests), inspect relevant screenshots under app/test-results, and attach evidence to the review task. Do not infer visual acceptance from tests alone.","Use deterministic provider/fixtures for tests. No external model use is needed to prove the planning CRUD and review workflow.","Run focused Harness/MCP/relational contributor tests in addition to active app checks for touched packages; declare and validate the necessary build/dependency composition explicitly. Source inspection is not runtime proof.","View/reference/comparison contracts: read-only nodes, applicability/default selection, explicit requested view precedence, decentralized graph serialization round trip, shared identity, immutable target resolution after restart/rebinding, explicit missing context, historical edits prohibited and field/relation comparisons.","Unified check evaluation: stale evidence, open/reopened/new comments, absent required actor outcome and requirement changes cannot bypass frozen submitted-policy checks.","Handoff fidelity includes full global specification and annotated image assets, not just task fields. Before R02 test browser approval with an authenticated test human principal and deny MCP/agent attempts to claim the human identity.","Passed review rejects new comments/reply/reopen/outcome changes; a fresh linked review preserves its history. Priority insertion with membership is atomic; there is no transient empty persisted bracket.","Check discovery/aggregation tests cover repository-specific selection, unsupported selectors, run granularity, missing definitions, source revisions, skipped execution, report availability and explicit human-only stale-evidence acceptance.","Review preparation/submission, feedback-row mutation and root-discussion closure, exact diff anchors, all/modified toggle, multi-iteration composition, Preview target validity, active-run cancellation and stable tab/view switching have focused domain and browser acceptance tests.","Graph fixtures assert actual IDs/edge sets independently of layout, then screenshot/interaction checks assert downward-return geometry, every range cap, queue range, independent branches and no connection above the abandoned endpoint.","Check outcome/freeze transition table and explicit review prerequisite replacement: same obligation/policy, listed pending dependants only, restart/idempotency, retained rejection history, unresolved root comments carried and overlapping freezes preserved.","Validate shared icon-only controls expose keyboard focus, accessible action names and tooltips sourced from operation metadata; screenshots cannot establish accessibility. Existing review checkpoint test:all remains a repository verification requirement, not a new default policy making all user full-suite checks mandatory.","Visual acceptance checks enforce final annotations against actual reusable components: ordinary Runnables tree row and correctly scoped inner splitter/toolbar bounds, rather than copying screenshot artifacts."],"implementationNotes":["The user explicitly requires reusing the relational operation/Harness/MCP architecture. The earlier blanket exclusion of Systems does not justify bypassing these requested components; reuse only the necessary contracts/packages, not obsolete apps or bookkeeping.","T01 resolves single ownership between active app task/session records and a planning contributor, then T02 exposes contributor-owned operations and Agent usage through the existing plugin. Do not keep two authoritative task representations or implement a CLI replacement.","Audit registered reusable components before each UI feature. Reuse first, rework second, add a shared component only for a documented gap. The user has explicitly endorsed that approach and rejected custom UI specific to this surface.","The task graph renderer must be a reusable relational presentation component consuming task/edge/range data and selection callbacks. Domain policy, persistence and review logic belong to their owners. Its initial consumer being this task surface does not justify task-specific controls inside it.","Record forms, relationship pickers, state commands, ordered priorities, history/evidence and threads require the same component audit. Existing schema-form, tree, splitter and shared element contracts are the starting point.","Shared-checkout review freezes remain a real execution constraint. Surface them accurately; independent graph branches do not make simultaneous writes to the same checkout safe. Automatic worktree/session orchestration is deferred.","Remove replaced sample fallbacks and obsolete paths as their replacement becomes usable. Preserve unrelated user changes and inventory user-authored data before any storage replacement. No silent resets or permanent legacy adapters.","V01 image review precedes implementation. R01 reviews those images plus operation parity and component ownership. Simple ergonomics are acceptable; incomplete CRUD is not.","Exact table internals, existing decentralized graph serialization and component exports are implementation investigations, not reasons to ask the user to design a solution. Document evidence before rework; user has authorized shared reuse/rework/addition.","Visual acceptance is explicitly recorded. The requested plan-review loop has converged and the final question is resolved; do not reopen accepted design solely because images contain minor glyph noise.","Existing terminal passed-review behavior is retained: later concerns use a fresh related review task. No question about post-pass thread reopening remains unless the user asks to change that existing contract.","Map descriptive purposes to shared graph presentation metadata: planning/replanning to lavender, review to sage, integration to tan, queue episodes gray, development/design/investigation/research/execution to teal, unknown neutral. These are presentation categories, not new entity types or a closed task-purpose vocabulary."],"updatedOn":"2026-09-27","userClarifications":["Manual queueing without automatic execution is accepted until session/agent management matures.","Contributor-owned relational operations exposed through the existing Broccoli Local plugin and MCP contributor are required in the MVP. A standalone CLI replacement is rejected.","Every supported planning CRUD operation must be available to the user in the UI as well as to the agent through tools. Ergonomics can be simple; independent user contribution is required.","Maximize reuse, then rework, then additions to shared components. No custom UI implementation specific to this surface.","Review coherent MVP screenshots, including contextual CRUD views, before implementation. Image review addresses ergonomics; operation parity still needs an explicit coverage checklist and tests.","MVP task editing uses a single freeform description, displayed URLs, flat relation lists including parent, exposed toolbar actions and top revision selection. Remove the task State field from Node; preserve placement operations elsewhere for CRUD parity.","Graph connectors have no arrowheads; range labels are plain and unboxed, nesting uses > without child counts, purpose colors stay consistent and inspector receives about two-thirds of the width.","Generic view name is Node. Reflect existing typed fields and relations and expose only allowed operations; support read-only nodes. Creator belongs in relations.","Duration and cost are wholly excluded from MVP, including placeholders. Graph remains schematic and distinguishes planned/recorded work.","Reviews are passing checks: automated runs, deterministic conditions, semantic reviewer decisions and discussion closure belong to one collection with adapted presentations. Outcome performs the transition; remove Action column and Edit button.","Revision selection gains no/inline/side-by-side comparison with an explicit base. Persisted graph links retain identity through the existing decentralized serialization contracts; the URL UI component is deferred.","Use a shared view matching contract over existing types/fields/relations as a transitional implementation; leave ECS undecided. Board column composition must preserve independent content and scrolling while reusing table-header work.","Repository checks detection/aggregation is the first MVP part. Shared check infrastructure is separately tracked as B01, not an MVP dependency.","One granular run-checks tool should resolve what to run; a discovery/read tool can coexist. Applicability is provided by checks, not a generic system decision.","Show what ran, results, when and the checked revision. Human may accept earlier passed evidence after changes; agent may skip rerunning but cannot hide the skip or treat stale results as fresh.","Agent reviews are deferred. Coverage visibility should include available results, thresholds/provenance and covered scope; advanced reusable coverage policy belongs to the follow-up.","MVP coverage shows the result and threshold only. Line-by-line source coverage and detailed file/function exploration are explicitly outside MVP and can grow later.","User explicitly confirmed the design is good enough in the final annotation message, subject to the listed small corrections and a final plan-only review. This closes visual approval; it does not claim any implementation exists.","Each work iteration after review and each review is a separate task; continuation/responds-to/reviews relations identify their lineage. Folded return-loop layout must not fabricate a cyclic task model.","The selected Review view has Overview, Changes and Preview tabs inside its shared toolbar; the graph remains mounted when changing tabs.","Author preparation, multi-row comment/reply controls and nested selected check execution are MVP requirements, not decorative mockup content.","Final annotations are tracked as authoritative corrections without another image generation. Runnables is a normal tree row, its buttons remain at the right, and the inner splitter must not cross the shared view-tools panel.","URL UI is explicitly deferred. The only retained link requirement is durable reference integrity on deserialization using the existing decentralized graph serialization format, verified rather than assumed.","Latest delivery authorization: complete software design with independent review, implementation with independent review, then leave the real MVP running. Intermediate R02 approval is independent-agent verification for this delivery; R03 remains human in-app acceptance."],"parity":[{"area":"Tasks","operations":"Create/read/update/delete; title-only task and one freeform description","ui":"Shared record form and command actions","tool":"Owning relational task operations"},{"area":"Relationships","operations":"Add/change/remove mutable parent, prerequisites and input/evidence links; inspect incoming references and immutable creator relation","ui":"Shared relationship editor and reference picker","tool":"Same relationship operations"},{"area":"Inputs","operations":"Create/read/update/delete; evidence and reported classification; many-to-many task linking","ui":"Shared input form and relationship editor","tool":"Same input operations"},{"area":"Queue and state","operations":"Move/return/block/complete/abandon; atomically insert a priority bracket with selected task(s), reorder brackets and remove a bracket by moving its members","ui":"Shared state controls, ordered groups and command actions","tool":"Same state/priority operations"},{"area":"Work evidence","operations":"Record/update allowed manual work/results; attach/detach evidence; inspect immutable history","ui":"Shared event/result form, evidence picker and history view","tool":"Same attempt/result/evidence operations"},{"area":"Reviews","operations":"Draft/configure/submit; exact targets; create distinct next work/review tasks with lineage; comment/reply multi-row CRUD; author close/reopen; permitted outcomes","ui":"Shared Review tabs, grouped-feedback component, Author readiness and Checks tree; Node for pre-submission relations","tool":"Same review operations with identical authority restrictions"},{"area":"Plan transfer","operations":"Import dry-run/apply; export; inspect receipt","ui":"Shared import/export command form","tool":"Same import/export operations"},{"area":"Node inspection and context","operations":"Read field/relation metadata and revisions; compare node revisions; enumerate supported views; inspect/resolve durable serialized graph references","ui":"Shared Node renderer, revision comparison controls, view matching and existing reference navigation","tool":"Owning node/history operations and existing graph serialization/reference resolution contracts"},{"area":"Repository check execution","operations":"Discover/read; run all/mandatory/selected at bounded granularity; stop scoped active runs; inspect nested latest results/provenance; human stale-passed-evidence acceptance","ui":"Shared check controls/results, report links and actor-permitted evidence acceptance","tool":"One owning run-checks operation with optional discovery/read; same actor rules"}],"imageReview":[{"id":"V1","label":"Task node and relations","surface":"Board with selected task","coverage":"Task URL, title, creator (must move to relations), one description and flat relations including parent. Revision and action tools at top. Placement commands still require an independent parity check.","path":"C:/Users/vince/.codex/visualizations/2026/09/21/01a0c5f4-7593-7072-8985-289e55a9faf9/mvp-plan/images/V1-revision-2.png","status":"accepted-direction-with-written-corrections","knownMismatches":["Toolbar should say Node, not Definition or a task-specific generic label.","Creator must move from its separate property row into flat relations.","URL/locator UI pictured here is superseded by explicit deferral. Reuse existing reference navigation and verify serialized graph links; do not implement a new address component from these pixels.","Add explicit comparison base and the shared no-diff / inline-diff / side-by-side controls.","Headers illustrate appearance only; reusable table-header/independent-column composition is not proven.","Placement/delete/import paths are not all pictured; operation parity remains mandatory."]},{"id":"V2","label":"Input capture and task linking","surface":"Board with selected input","coverage":"Input create/edit/delete, reported classification and evidence, link existing tasks or create investigation; no implied confirmation.","path":"C:/Users/vince/.codex/visualizations/2026/09/21/01a0c5f4-7593-7072-8985-289e55a9faf9/mvp-plan/images/V2-revision-2.png","status":"accepted-direction-with-written-corrections","knownMismatches":["Toolbar should say Node, not Definition or a task-specific generic label.","Creator must move from its separate property row into flat relations.","URL/locator UI pictured here is superseded by explicit deferral. Reuse existing reference navigation and verify serialized graph links; do not implement a new address component from these pixels.","Add explicit comparison base and the shared no-diff / inline-diff / side-by-side controls.","Reported classification is a claim, not confirmed truth. Metadata type rendering/permissions must come from the node contract."]},{"id":"V3","label":"Plan and record nested work","surface":"Task graph with selected task/attempt","coverage":"Same record/relationship components as V1 with session ranges, diff/result links, plain task graph ranges ; timing/cost placeholders must be removed.","path":"C:/Users/vince/.codex/visualizations/2026/09/21/01a0c5f4-7593-7072-8985-289e55a9faf9/mvp-plan/images/V3-revision-2.png","status":"accepted-direction-with-written-corrections","knownMismatches":["Toolbar should say Node, not Definition or a task-specific generic label.","Creator must move from its separate property row into flat relations.","URL/locator UI pictured here is superseded by explicit deferral. Reuse existing reference navigation and verify serialized graph links; do not implement a new address component from these pixels.","Add explicit comparison base and the shared no-diff / inline-diff / side-by-side controls.","Remove Duration and Cost entirely, including dash placeholders.","Use Node for generic inspection; retain Work only if it later has a distinct supported purpose, not as a redundant MVP view.","Graph is a schematic example; exact planned/recorded state and chronology must come from data. No scaled time claims.","Divider is about37/63, implementation starts1/3 versus2/3. Save styling differs from other mockups: normalize shared toolbar.","Old graph layout is superseded by final Overview/Changes references: distinct-task folded review loops, endpoint caps, gray queue ranges and terminal abandonment are mandatory."]},{"id":"V4","label":"Review Overview, accepted final hierarchy","surface":"Selected review task; Overview tab","coverage":"Author draft submission; reusable feedback rows; activity evidence; Checks with Reviewers then Runnables, each Mandatory/Optional; header-only granular execution.","path":"C:/Users/vince/.codex/visualizations/2026/09/21/01a0c5f4-7593-7072-8985-289e55a9faf9/mvp-plan/images/V4-overview-accepted.png","status":"accepted-direction-with-written-corrections","knownMismatches":["Text/glyph artifacts in file link and some icons are generation noise; use real readable labels and existing icon components.","Runnables is a child of Checks, alongside Reviewers, even where bitmap indentation is subtle; parent/child boundary is defined in the written tree contract.","Example authors, check results, times and graph actors are illustrative, not runtime evidence. Agent-review execution remains deferred; present already recorded participation only.","Minor top-border/spacing artifacts do not authorize a new layout; maintain consistent native panel borders and top margin with no bottom gap for tabs.","Controls must satisfy the acceptance scenarios; images do not prove author permissions, scope freeze, review passage or cancellation.","Final annotation 1 (85.4%,53%): Runnables is an ordinary nested bush row under Checks, with its four action buttons right-aligned on that row; do not reproduce the separate panel/header treatment.","Final annotation 2 (80.1%,8.5%): the inner Overview splitter must begin below the view-tools toolbar, not extend through it.","Final annotation 3 (99%,9.2%): the far-right tool belongs to the shared view-tools panel spanning both content subpanes. Do not create a separate sidebar toolbar/border. URL component behavior itself is deferred."]},{"id":"V5","label":"Review Changes and Preview entry","surface":"Selected review task; Changes tab","coverage":"All/modified files, exact diff, shared multirow comment/reply, one revision comparison control, Preview tab.","path":"C:/Users/vince/.codex/visualizations/2026/09/21/01a0c5f4-7593-7072-8985-289e55a9faf9/mvp-plan/images/V5-changes-accepted.png","status":"accepted-direction-with-written-corrections","knownMismatches":["Sample code/data are illustrative. Actual review uses immutable target manifest and persisted inputs.","Top-level feedback has minor residual left spacing in the bitmap; implementation aligns it with the full-width context body, with indent only for replies.","Preview tab presence is not proof of historical preview support; reuse existing renderer and explicitly report unsupported targets.","Iteration multiselection is required in the file-tree tools but not fully pictured; see Review target and changes."]}],"visualReview":{"date":"2026-09-27","findings":"UI-REVIEW.md","userApproved":true,"limits":"User explicitly accepted the design with final corrections. Static images remain imperfect references: written requirements override glyph/border artifacts; no runtime, accessibility, topology, reuse or CRUD correctness is proven by a bitmap."},"revision":"software-design-2-reviewed","reconciliation":{"baseline":{"file":"plan.json","lastWriteTime":"2026-09-27T03:04:19.8120879+02:00","source":"Filesystem last-write timestamp observed before this update; agrees with the preceding image-batch update in the conversation."},"precedence":"Latest explicit user decisions override older text and screenshots. Assistant implementation proposals are defaults for review, not evidence of user approval. Screenshot links illustrate layouts only; documented corrections take precedence.","iterations":[{"id":"D01","source":"User re-posted the earlier 13 annotations after a misclick.","change":"Confirmed all 13 were already covered. Preserve URLs over bare IDs, removal of redundant navigation/State, flat relations including parent, one description, direct toolbar actions, top revisions and omission of the duration breakdown. Timing placeholders were the baseline, now superseded by D04."},{"id":"D02","source":"Next image review: five task/board notes, two graph notes, four review notes and component-model observation.","change":"Creator is a read-only relation. Add revision comparison modes. Build a reusable contextual address component. Audit shared table headers/column composition. Correct planned-versus-recorded semantics. Unify reviewer decisions, automated results and discussion closure as checks. Remove separate reviewer Action/Edit UI. Review is a presentation of the same node. Broad ECS redesign remains deferred."},{"id":"D03","source":"Naming discussion: user chose Node after considering Properties, Inspector and Node editor.","change":"Use Node as the generic view name. It reflects declared fields/types and relations, respects supported operations and works for read-only nodes too; no capability is implied merely by the view name."},{"id":"D04","source":"User follow-up on column architecture, duration/cost and transitional view matching; subsequent agreement.","change":"Duration and cost are completely excluded from MVP, including fields and placeholders. Existing types/fields/relations supply view matching for now. Board container plus reusable independent columns is the working composition, subject to inspection of existing table internals; no common row grid."},{"id":"D05","source":"Current request to reconcile the plan and run an isolated iterative subagent review.","change":"Update the canonical plan and annotated screenshot references, then review only this plan with a fresh agent. Record discussions/dispositions between rounds. Do not implement the app in this planning turn."},{"id":"D06","source":"User asks whether local DNS can provide stable addresses and reaffirms unfinished Review right-panel design.","change":"Record local hostname plus fixed local reverse-proxy entry as a candidate, not an approved or configured solution. Restore explicit visual iteration/acceptance of the Review panel before implementation; technical plan review convergence does not settle design acceptance."},{"id":"D07","source":"Node-first image review, comments as input nodes, snapshot discussion and repository/shared-check needs analysis.","change":"Use one revision control; establish the generic Node view before returning to Review design. Comments are related input nodes, discussion structure is formed by relations, and check discovery does not require persisting every discovered check as an edge. MVP detects/aggregates repository checks and exposes a granular run tool. Shared/versioned cross-repository check infrastructure is a separate backlog task. Human judges stale-result applicability; no automatic semantic expiry exemption. Agent review is deferred."},{"id":"D08","source":"User separates temporal evidence from policy; requests Overview then Changes and explicit review/rework loops.","change":"Overview contains comment/check-run activity and author/check controls; Changes shows exact files/diffs with anchored discussions. Every post-review work iteration and each subsequent review is a distinct task. Layout folds a review end back down to the next task start; no Work/Review lane split or model cycles."},{"id":"D09","source":"Multiple feedback rows, preview, shared replies, author readiness and compact selectable checks.","change":"Shared comment/input presentation groups typed text rows, trash controls and footer actions; top-level context/preview uses full width and only replies indent. Draft preparation precedes submission. Exact worktree/revision context must back comments."},{"id":"D10","source":"Final two image annotation rounds, then explicit good-enough acceptance and request for clean-context success-criteria review.","change":"Checks contains Reviewers above Runnables; each contains Mandatory/Optional groups. Runnables has play-all/mandatory/selected/stop, no checkboxes or per-item play buttons. Latest results nest under checks. Add All files/Modified files and Preview. Correct range caps, gray queue episodes and branch wiring. User accepts the design with minor image noise; update plan and review before development."},{"id":"D11","source":"User final three annotations; explicitly skips image generation and defers URL UI.","change":"Runnables is an ordinary nested row in the Checks bush with its buttons right-aligned on that row. The Overview inner splitter begins below the shared view toolbar; the far-right link/tools belong to that toolbar. Treat screenshot borders/headers as anomalies, not implementation truth. URL UI and external opening are deferred; persisted links must resolve after deserialization using the existing decentralized graph serialization contracts. This resolves the last planning question."}],"latestBaseline":{"revision":"discussion-reconciliation-6-coverage-and-review-image","lastWriteTime":"2026-09-27T03:45:06.668Z","source":"Canonical plan immediately before final design reconciliation; earlier baseline retained as historical context."}},"componentPlan":[{"component":"Board and columns","basis":"Existing table-header contracts, tree/list primitives, splitter","work":"Inspect and reuse header controls; compose independent scrolling column components, unless current table natively supports independent contents without a common row grid."},{"component":"Node view","basis":"Existing schema-form and relational typed fields/edge descriptors","work":"Reflect supported fields and one flat relation list; renderer dispatch by declared type, read/write capabilities and actor permissions. Creator is an immutable relation. Unknown field types use a readable fallback without permitting unsupported edits."},{"component":"View selection","basis":"Existing view-toolbar","work":"Small declarative requirements contract plus one adapter for current types/relations/operations. No ECS framework."},{"component":"Revision comparison","basis":"Existing revision controls and three-way diff-mode buttons","work":"Shared node-scoped field/relation comparison over immutable revisions; compose the existing diff renderer where suitable."},{"component":"Persisted graph references","basis":"Existing decentralized graph serialization, node identity and reference resolution contracts","work":"Inspect/reuse owner contracts; validate complete round trips, shared reference identity, immutable target references, restart and unresolved targets. No new user-facing URL component, address codec or local DNS/proxy integration in MVP."},{"component":"Graph","basis":"Approved reusable relational graph renderer addition and splitter","work":"Project tasks